1
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:32,741
‎Gyro. About what Laurence Boomboom said...

2
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:37,828
‎You think we're the only ones
‎after your life?

3
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:41,540
‎You've got a bounty on your head.

4
00:00:41,541 --> 00:00:43,418
‎What was he talking about?

5
00:00:44,127 --> 00:00:46,503
‎I told you it's none of your business.

6
00:00:46,504 --> 00:00:48,047
‎No! Answer me!

7
00:00:48,631 --> 00:00:50,507
‎I have a right to know.

8
00:00:50,508 --> 00:00:52,552
‎I almost died because of it!

9
00:00:56,181 --> 00:00:58,015
‎So you're a judicial official?

10
00:00:58,016 --> 00:01:02,227
‎Was Robinson after your bounty too?

11
00:01:02,228 --> 00:01:06,024
‎Why did you enter this race? Answer me!

12
00:02:42,579 --> 00:02:47,125
‎#05 - THE TERRORIST
‎FROM A FARAWAY COUNTRY

13
00:02:52,088 --> 00:02:57,468
‎2ND STAGE DAY 6
‎MIDPOINT

14
00:03:04,851 --> 00:03:08,061
‎Welcome. You made excellent time.

15
00:03:08,062 --> 00:03:11,357
‎You're currently in fourth place,

16
00:03:12,025 --> 00:03:13,359
‎Mr. Oye.

17
00:03:18,489 --> 00:03:22,451
‎This town was built
‎as the race's midpoint.

18
00:03:22,452 --> 00:03:27,205
‎Reports say you're over a day ahead
‎of the groups around Sand Man and Dio

19
00:03:27,206 --> 00:03:29,666
‎on the other route.

20
00:03:29,667 --> 00:03:33,378
‎Fourth? I'm not in first?

21
00:03:33,379 --> 00:03:36,089
‎First place is Mr. Mountain Tim.

22
00:03:36,090 --> 00:03:41,178
‎But Mr. Gyro Zeppeli
‎claims he was a neck ahead.

23
00:03:41,179 --> 00:03:45,849
‎Mr. Johnny Joestar also insisted
‎he came in first.

24
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:52,105
‎But since this is only a checkpoint, it
‎doesn't affect the standings or records.

25
00:03:52,106 --> 00:03:53,191
‎That's right.

26
00:04:32,605 --> 00:04:36,651
‎I found a wax seal bearing
‎the royal coat of arms outside the hotel.

27
00:04:40,697 --> 00:04:41,864
‎There it is.

28
00:04:42,782 --> 00:04:46,202
‎So he did receive a letter
‎from the king's envoy.

29
00:04:49,497 --> 00:04:54,710
‎"Travel 30 miles north to the Red Canyon.
‎The Zombie Horse awaits you.

30
00:04:54,711 --> 00:04:55,961
‎Take it.

31
00:04:55,962 --> 00:05:00,299
‎The Zombie Horse has the power
‎to alleviate weariness and injury.

32
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:02,010
‎It will serve you well."

33
00:05:03,219 --> 00:05:05,095
‎What's the Zombie Horse?

34
00:05:05,096 --> 00:05:07,264
‎Do I know you?

35
00:05:07,265 --> 00:05:09,850
‎Oh! Guess I was wrong!

36
00:05:09,851 --> 00:05:13,604
‎Then why are you in someone else's room,
‎going through his things?

37
00:05:15,773 --> 00:05:18,775
‎I'm looking for Gyro Zeppeli. Where is he?

38
00:05:18,776 --> 00:05:22,988
‎Well, here's an idiot
‎who can't hold a conversation.

39
00:05:22,989 --> 00:05:26,158
‎You know answering a question
‎with a question

40
00:05:26,159 --> 00:05:29,328
‎gets you an F, genius?

41
00:05:29,329 --> 00:05:32,456
‎I need to find Gyro Zeppeli.
‎Is he in the stable?

42
00:05:32,457 --> 00:05:35,168
‎Hey! Are you screwing with me?

43
00:05:41,132 --> 00:05:43,468
‎Oh, here's a word of warning.

44
00:05:44,052 --> 00:05:47,387
‎Don't let go of my skin yet.

45
00:05:47,388 --> 00:05:49,431
‎I'm about to step away.

46
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:51,893
‎Don't spread your fingers. It's dangerous.

47
00:05:58,441 --> 00:06:05,198
‎Too bad. I told you not to spread
‎your fingers once you touched me.

48
00:06:08,993 --> 00:06:12,246
‎I won't spare anyone
‎who rides for the king.

49
00:06:13,081 --> 00:06:16,459
‎You'll die,
‎Judicial Official Gyro Zeppeli.

50
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:22,256
‎What's that sound?

51
00:06:25,259 --> 00:06:28,220
‎An explosion! Get the fire pumps!

52
00:06:28,221 --> 00:06:30,680
‎Get the hoses from the water tank!

53
00:06:30,681 --> 00:06:32,224
‎What the...

54
00:06:32,225 --> 00:06:33,851
‎What happened?

55
00:06:42,151 --> 00:06:44,152
‎This can't be...

56
00:06:44,153 --> 00:06:45,530
‎Mountain Tim!

57
00:06:55,832 --> 00:06:57,833
‎Mountain Tim!

58
00:06:57,834 --> 00:07:02,295
‎He's alive! He tore his body apart
‎with his rope!

59
00:07:02,296 --> 00:07:05,383
‎Don't come... Gyro...

60
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:07,843
‎This explosion...

61
00:07:07,844 --> 00:07:09,177
‎What was that?

62
00:07:09,178 --> 00:07:12,640
‎Stay back! He's hiding nearby!

63
00:07:13,182 --> 00:07:15,143
‎It's a Stand ability!

64
00:07:28,781 --> 00:07:31,575
‎He's here! Don't let him touch you!

65
00:07:31,576 --> 00:07:33,786
‎He's the enemy! Run!

66
00:07:37,582 --> 00:07:41,002
‎What the hell is that cowboy?

67
00:07:41,711 --> 00:07:44,464
‎What's he made of?

68
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:48,550
‎Long time no see, Gyro Zeppeli.

69
00:07:48,551 --> 00:07:50,302
‎You...

70
00:07:50,303 --> 00:07:54,181
‎Damn it! Gyro, he touched you!

71
00:07:54,182 --> 00:07:57,185
‎He just touched you with his finger!

72
00:08:00,563 --> 00:08:03,023
‎What the hell is this?

73
00:08:03,024 --> 00:08:05,775
‎-He's stuck a pin on you!
‎-A pin?

74
00:08:05,776 --> 00:08:07,944
‎That's his ability!

75
00:08:07,945 --> 00:08:11,781
‎Hold them down!
‎If they pop out, they'll explode!

76
00:08:11,782 --> 00:08:13,241
‎What?

77
00:08:13,242 --> 00:08:15,911
‎Just do it! Hold them down!

78
00:08:15,912 --> 00:08:17,329
‎It's what happened to me!

79
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:19,916
‎When they popped out, they exploded!

80
00:08:23,711 --> 00:08:26,338
‎What, you're telling him?

81
00:08:26,339 --> 00:08:29,591
‎Don't let go! That's the rule!

82
00:08:29,592 --> 00:08:31,427
‎They are like land mines!

83
00:08:31,552 --> 00:08:36,140
‎When they pop out, your hand will explode!

84
00:08:36,807 --> 00:08:41,353
‎These watch-like rings
‎are fused to my fingers.

85
00:08:41,354 --> 00:08:44,105
‎They even look like real mechanisms!

86
00:08:44,106 --> 00:08:45,608
‎That's a Stand!

87
00:08:47,235 --> 00:08:50,403
‎A Stand is a manifestation
‎of spiritual energy.

88
00:08:50,404 --> 00:08:55,826
‎It manifests from within us
‎and can inflict real damage!

89
00:08:56,327 --> 00:08:58,621
‎Even that explosion
‎comes from that energy!

90
00:09:01,290 --> 00:09:04,709
‎Gyro! He said, "Long time no see."

91
00:09:04,710 --> 00:09:06,337
‎Do you know him?

92
00:09:07,004 --> 00:09:09,549
‎Yeah. His name is Oye.

93
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:15,929
‎He's a terrorist who bombed
‎the king's carriage two years ago

94
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:20,308
‎The king wasn't aboard,
‎but five bystanders were killed.

95
00:09:20,309 --> 00:09:22,394
‎Two of them were children!

96
00:09:22,395 --> 00:09:25,313
‎He was captured and sentenced to death,

97
00:09:25,314 --> 00:09:29,277
‎but he planted hidden explosives
‎in a guard's ear and blew him up.

98
00:09:29,402 --> 00:09:30,486
‎Then he escaped!

99
00:09:31,612 --> 00:09:34,073
‎How's your old man?

100
00:09:34,824 --> 00:09:39,661
‎I hear he's retired,
‎and you've taken his place as executioner.

101
00:09:39,662 --> 00:09:40,871
‎Executioner?

102
00:09:43,916 --> 00:09:49,379
‎My father should've taken your head
‎when he had the chance.

103
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:51,673
‎Too bad.

104
00:09:51,674 --> 00:09:55,093
‎My passing through Arizona was God's will.

105
00:09:55,094 --> 00:09:57,053
‎Even I was surprised.

106
00:09:57,054 --> 00:10:01,433
‎My talent with explosives
‎became an ability within me.

107
00:10:01,434 --> 00:10:03,893
‎You passed through the Devil's Palm?

108
00:10:03,894 --> 00:10:07,773
‎I took it as a mission from God!

109
00:10:09,775 --> 00:10:12,861
‎Gyro, one more thing.

110
00:10:12,862 --> 00:10:16,157
‎The quickest way
‎to stop a Stand ability is...

111
00:10:16,907 --> 00:10:20,661
‎Once the user dies,
‎and the ability dies with him!

112
00:10:21,329 --> 00:10:24,665
‎That's awfully nice of you
‎to explain all that.

113
00:10:25,166 --> 00:10:28,669
‎But I've already taken
‎his right hand out of play.

114
00:10:29,837 --> 00:10:31,213
‎You know what?

115
00:10:32,256 --> 00:10:38,179
‎It's like a man drowning in debt
‎turning to loan sharks.

116
00:10:41,515 --> 00:10:43,726
‎There's no way out!

117
00:10:46,979 --> 00:10:48,189
‎A rat?

118
00:10:48,856 --> 00:10:51,566
‎Stay away from the rat!
‎Don't let it near you!

119
00:10:51,567 --> 00:10:53,402
‎It's a bomb now!

120
00:11:04,997 --> 00:11:06,956
‎Gyro! Don't let go!

121
00:11:06,957 --> 00:11:08,751
‎Don't even move your fingers!

122
00:11:14,757 --> 00:11:17,384
‎The pin popped out! Gyro, grab it!

123
00:11:17,385 --> 00:11:19,344
‎The pin came out of your hand!

124
00:11:19,345 --> 00:11:22,473
‎Put it back! Stick it back
‎where it came out!

125
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:27,477
‎Didn't it come out of your palm?

126
00:11:27,478 --> 00:11:30,940
‎Isn't it on the palm side,
‎where you're gripping the Steel Ball?

127
00:11:32,775 --> 00:11:35,860
‎Just put it back! It'll explode!

128
00:11:35,861 --> 00:11:38,363
‎No! It's on the palm side!

129
00:11:38,364 --> 00:11:42,993
‎If he makes room to put it back,
‎more pins will pop out!

130
00:11:57,508 --> 00:11:59,427
‎From the back of his hand...

131
00:12:07,226 --> 00:12:08,310
‎He got it back in.

132
00:12:08,978 --> 00:12:12,022
‎You did it! It didn't explode!

133
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:18,153
‎That really had me sweating.

134
00:12:18,154 --> 00:12:21,823
‎It's been four days
‎since I gained this ability in the desert.

135
00:12:21,824 --> 00:12:26,537
‎Now I understand everything
‎about my ability.

136
00:12:28,372 --> 00:12:32,376
‎God's power has no weaknesses.

137
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:37,464
‎Do your best to keep those pins
‎from popping out.

138
00:12:37,465 --> 00:12:40,885
‎Gyro! Johnny! Don't let him get away!

139
00:12:41,594 --> 00:12:43,928
‎Get away?

140
00:12:43,929 --> 00:12:46,222
‎It's already over.

141
00:12:46,223 --> 00:12:48,975
‎Gyro won't make it three more steps.

142
00:12:48,976 --> 00:12:52,354
‎His hands are only going to get sweatier!

143
00:12:54,899 --> 00:12:57,818
‎Stay back, Johnny! Don't come near me!

144
00:12:59,111 --> 00:13:00,653
‎You're sweating!

145
00:13:00,654 --> 00:13:02,572
‎You noticed?

146
00:13:02,573 --> 00:13:07,368
‎Anything that his hand touches
‎will make the pins pop out.

147
00:13:07,369 --> 00:13:10,121
‎Damn it! This is impossible.

148
00:13:10,122 --> 00:13:13,583
‎What do I do? The more I hold them,
‎the more I sweat!

149
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:15,793
‎More pins are coming out!

150
00:13:15,794 --> 00:13:17,086
‎Wipe it off, Gyro!

151
00:13:17,087 --> 00:13:20,423
‎No! The sweat and the pins
‎are stuck together.

152
00:13:20,424 --> 00:13:22,342
‎They keep flowing out!

153
00:13:22,343 --> 00:13:23,426
‎Damn it!

154
00:13:23,427 --> 00:13:25,845
‎I've got to take him down.

155
00:13:25,846 --> 00:13:29,265
‎I'll throw this Steel Ball and finish him!

156
00:13:29,266 --> 00:13:33,269
‎I see. That might work.

157
00:13:33,270 --> 00:13:36,898
‎If your right hand
‎is going to blow off anyway,

158
00:13:36,899 --> 00:13:39,610
‎you might as well take your shot
‎and throw it.

159
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:43,697
‎But the moment you let go,
‎it'll blow to pieces.

160
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:03,968
‎Gyro!

161
00:14:04,552 --> 00:14:06,844
‎The blast shifted.

162
00:14:06,845 --> 00:14:09,305
‎I'll take that bastard out.

163
00:14:09,306 --> 00:14:12,226
‎Better than losing my arm!

164
00:14:15,271 --> 00:14:16,730
‎You did it!

165
00:14:20,818 --> 00:14:22,902
‎You're not getting away, Oye!

166
00:14:22,903 --> 00:14:24,863
‎Are you going after him?

167
00:14:24,864 --> 00:14:28,825
‎The one the letter said... He's after it.

168
00:14:28,826 --> 00:14:29,909
‎After what?

169
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:32,203
‎It's the king's gift.

170
00:14:32,204 --> 00:14:34,414
‎The Zombie Horse at Red Canyon.

171
00:14:34,415 --> 00:14:35,623
‎The Zombie Horse?

172
00:14:35,624 --> 00:14:38,376
‎I can't let him have it.

173
00:14:38,377 --> 00:14:42,715
‎The horse which alleviates weariness
‎and even injuries!

174
00:14:46,302 --> 00:14:48,679
‎I'll get it before he does.

175
00:14:53,517 --> 00:14:54,935
‎[STAND NAME] TIC TAC BOOM
‎[STAND MASTER] OYE

176
00:15:04,945 --> 00:15:07,906
‎Johnny. He's my enemy.

177
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:12,160
‎This is between him, me, and my country.
‎It has nothing to do with you.

178
00:15:12,161 --> 00:15:14,787
‎I don't know what happened to you.

179
00:15:14,788 --> 00:15:16,706
‎You don't have to tell me.

180
00:15:16,707 --> 00:15:19,376
‎But I'm coming with you, of course!

181
00:15:21,670 --> 00:15:25,757
‎I don't take orders,
‎and I don't need help.

182
00:15:25,758 --> 00:15:29,677
‎But you've dragged me into this
‎since the starting line.

183
00:15:29,678 --> 00:15:31,639
‎It's too late to split up now!

184
00:15:32,848 --> 00:15:34,141
‎Suit yourself.

185
00:15:43,692 --> 00:15:46,319
‎They've figured out my ability.

186
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:50,240
‎Now I need to understand Gyro Zeppeli's.

187
00:15:50,866 --> 00:15:53,577
‎What's the range
‎of his Steel Ball attack?

188
00:15:54,286 --> 00:15:56,997
‎Judging by that throw,
‎it's about 20 yards.

189
00:15:57,665 --> 00:16:02,711
‎Any closer and he'll get me.
‎Any farther, and my explosions won't work.

190
00:16:03,712 --> 00:16:07,591
‎I have to attack
‎from just beyond his range.

191
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:14,974
‎He's pouring water from his canteen.

192
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:26,985
‎Gyro! Get out of the water!

193
00:16:26,986 --> 00:16:29,696
‎He's turned the water into bombs!

194
00:16:29,697 --> 00:16:33,783
‎There are pins in the water! Get to shore!

195
00:16:33,784 --> 00:16:36,870
‎No. You get to shore alone.

196
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:41,500
‎I'll do the opposite. I'll keep running
‎and catch up to him.

197
00:16:44,586 --> 00:16:45,879
‎Wait, Gyro!

198
00:16:49,758 --> 00:16:50,801
‎There you are.

199
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:06,816
‎Even if we touch his land-mine pins,

200
00:17:06,817 --> 00:17:09,610
‎the explosion won't come
‎until a moment later.

201
00:17:09,611 --> 00:17:13,282
‎We'll speed up
‎and make it explode behind us!

202
00:17:15,826 --> 00:17:17,910
‎We're pushing through!

203
00:17:17,911 --> 00:17:20,621
‎It's worse to leave the river
‎and slow down!

204
00:17:20,622 --> 00:17:23,166
‎Don't let the horses hesitate!

205
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:25,961
‎I'll get close
‎and slam the Steel Ball into him!

206
00:17:30,883 --> 00:17:32,800
‎Gyro Zeppeli...

207
00:17:32,801 --> 00:17:34,469
‎You're getting cocky.

208
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:36,095
‎Knew you'd speed up.

209
00:17:36,096 --> 00:17:39,557
‎I'm not running from you.

210
00:17:39,558 --> 00:17:42,560
‎I'm herding you into this river!

211
00:17:42,561 --> 00:17:44,521
‎It's a waterfall, Gyro!

212
00:17:49,318 --> 00:17:50,611
‎Push through!

213
00:17:51,278 --> 00:17:55,282
‎Don't slow down!
‎Make it up, just like he did!

214
00:18:10,506 --> 00:18:13,133
‎Wasps! They're coming at us!

215
00:18:13,717 --> 00:18:16,678
‎Every wasp has a pin on it!

216
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:20,973
‎We'll have to cut them down one by one!

217
00:18:20,974 --> 00:18:22,810
‎With my fingernail shots!

218
00:18:31,485 --> 00:18:33,487
‎I'll hit him from here!

219
00:18:36,907 --> 00:18:40,702
‎Forty yards! It won't be fatal.

220
00:18:41,495 --> 00:18:44,163
‎My explosions are stronger!

221
00:18:44,164 --> 00:18:47,376
‎You'll be the ones
‎to take the wasps and blow up!

222
00:18:53,715 --> 00:18:55,967
‎The wasps hit the spider web.

223
00:18:55,968 --> 00:18:57,344
‎Get down, Johnny!

224
00:19:06,019 --> 00:19:08,814
‎Yes! We made it up the falls!

225
00:19:16,655 --> 00:19:17,823
‎Gyro!

226
00:19:20,868 --> 00:19:23,787
‎This... This smell...

227
00:19:26,748 --> 00:19:27,958
‎Johnny! Stop!

228
00:19:29,042 --> 00:19:30,043
‎Don't move.

229
00:19:31,003 --> 00:19:32,004
‎What's this?

230
00:19:37,634 --> 00:19:39,177
‎Don't touch the smoke.

231
00:19:39,178 --> 00:19:42,222
‎Don't open your mouth. Don't inhale.
‎Hold your breath!

232
00:19:42,973 --> 00:19:45,183
‎Don't let the horses breathe either!

233
00:19:45,184 --> 00:19:46,684
‎What?

234
00:19:46,685 --> 00:19:48,728
‎Hold your breath?

235
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:51,648
‎Impossible. Not while you're alive.

236
00:19:52,149 --> 00:19:56,903
‎Did you think all I sent at you
‎was water and wasps?

237
00:19:56,904 --> 00:19:59,530
‎Even what I breathe in and breathe out!

238
00:19:59,531 --> 00:20:02,492
‎Anything I touch can become a land mine!

239
00:20:05,078 --> 00:20:09,790
‎You're like rats
‎trapped in a cage over a fire.

240
00:20:09,791 --> 00:20:13,253
‎There's no escape left.
‎There's nothing you can do!

241
00:20:15,923 --> 00:20:19,508
‎God has granted me an incredible ability.

242
00:20:19,509 --> 00:20:24,389
‎When I return home, I'll assassinate
‎even the king with this ability!

243
00:20:34,691 --> 00:20:38,110
‎If we don't finish him, it's over.

244
00:20:38,111 --> 00:20:40,530
‎But where is he?

245
00:20:44,576 --> 00:20:45,577
‎Gyro!

246
00:20:46,161 --> 00:20:48,497
‎It should explode any second now.

247
00:20:57,673 --> 00:20:58,715
‎This is...

248
00:20:59,925 --> 00:21:02,511
‎The wasps that got caught on that thread?

249
00:21:03,262 --> 00:21:05,221
‎You're dreaming!

250
00:21:05,222 --> 00:21:10,434
‎You think wasps I made into mines
‎can really blow me up?

251
00:21:10,435 --> 00:21:12,354
‎I'll rip it apart!

252
00:21:15,107 --> 00:21:16,857
‎What's this?

253
00:21:16,858 --> 00:21:20,195
‎They're not wasps... They're spinning.

254
00:21:27,494 --> 00:21:29,078
‎There you are!

255
00:21:29,079 --> 00:21:33,416
‎You mistook the sound of
‎Johnny's spinning nails for a wasp.

256
00:21:33,417 --> 00:21:36,502
‎Then you pulled it in
‎to cut the spider's thread.

257
00:21:36,503 --> 00:21:39,422
‎So now I know where you are!

258
00:21:39,423 --> 00:21:41,216
‎One more!

259
00:21:52,769 --> 00:21:55,772
‎-Let's keep charging through, Johnny.
‎-Right!

260
00:21:56,565 --> 00:21:59,651
‎We're still first and second!

261
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:01,737
‎That's us!

262
00:23:30,992 --> 00:23:35,997
‎Subtitle translation by: Ryoko Quirke
